From 0eb2651bdf5d25a017f529518b6cf5f1bbc697cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sabith Saheb <shabi7204192361@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:33:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] rsa_kem: check secretlen before writing the RSASVE secret

rsasve_generate() writes nlen = RSA_size() bytes of the random secret z
into the caller's secret buffer and then reads them back
for RSA_public_encrypt(), but it only checks the wrapped key buffer size
against nlen.  EVP_PKEY_encapsulate(3) documents *genkeylen as the size
of the provided buffer, so a caller passing a secret buffer smaller than
the modulus, e.g. 32 bytes with an RSA-2048 key, gets a heap buffer
overflow of up to RSA_size() - *secretlen bytes in BN_bn2binpad().

The EC, ECX, ML-KEM and hybrid ML-KEM encapsulate paths already reject
a *secretlen smaller than the secret they produce. Do the same for RSASVE,
next to the existing outlen check. A NULL secretlen is still accepted
as before.

Add a too-short secretlen case to kem_rsa_gen_recover
in evp_libctx_test.

Fixes: 80f4fd18f72c "Add KEM (Key encapsulation mechanism) support to providers"
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Reviewed-by: Tomas Mraz <tomas@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Wed Nov 25 15:48:53 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33328
(cherry picked from commit 6a9d4acb5f7c70b310d27ed494f5d626e2d3950f)
---
 providers/implementations/kem/rsa_kem.c |  9 +++++++++
 test/evp_libctx_test.c                  | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/providers/implementations/kem/rsa_kem.c b/providers/implementations/kem/rsa_kem.c
index 47f0c80c9443..f4c3a0d0c7d1 100644
--- a/providers/implementations/kem/rsa_kem.c
+++ b/providers/implementations/kem/rsa_kem.c
@@ -321,6 +321,15 @@ static int rsasve_generate(PROV_RSA_CTX *prsactx,
         return 0;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Likewise, if secretlen is specified it must report the length of the
+     * secret buffer, which receives nlen bytes
+     */
+    if (secretlen != NULL && *secretlen < nlen) {
+        ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_PROV, PROV_R_INVALID_OUTPUT_LENGTH);
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     /*
      * Step (2): Generate a random byte string z of nlen bytes where
      *            1 < z < n - 1
diff --git a/test/evp_libctx_test.c b/test/evp_libctx_test.c
index e65578e70501..df6a39187a40 100644
--- a/test/evp_libctx_test.c
+++ b/test/evp_libctx_test.c
@@ -628,6 +628,16 @@ static int kem_rsa_gen_recover(void)
             ret = 0;
     }
 
+    /* Test that providing a too short secretlen fails */
+    if (fips_provider_version_match(libctx, ">=4.2.0")) {
+        ctlen = sizeof(ct);
+        secretlen = 32;
+        if (!TEST_int_eq(EVP_PKEY_encapsulate(dctx, ct, &ctlen, secret,
+                             &secretlen),
+                0))
+            ret = 0;
+    }
+
     EVP_PKEY_free(pub);
     EVP_PKEY_free(priv);
     EVP_PKEY_CTX_free(rctx);
